crypto.rs adapts selected BAC KDF, 3DES-CBC, ISO9797 method-2 padding and
retail-MAC primitives. The application owns the bounded reader and TD3 parser.
Compared with the referenced controller: verify mutual-authentication MACs and
both nonces before accepting keys, use constant-time comparisons, reject duplicate
or unknown/out-of-order secure-response objects, enforce canonical lengths, reject
SSC overflow, remove null/unprotected sessions, and zeroize transient buffers.
Native Android BAC-enabled TD3 DG1 and bounded EF.SOD reads are connected.
The locally implemented RFC 5652 verifier checks DG1/SOD signatures. A bounded
offline Japanese CSCA/CRL verifier follows ICAO Part 12; inputs and pins are
documented in crates/identity/src/passport/trust/README.md. Full Passive Authentication, PACE, photos and
passport issuance remain unqualified.
The Wallet may explicitly save matched document number and MRZ in its encrypted
account collection. Keys, counters, nonces and transport bytes are never persisted.
Protocol and known-answer tests: ICAO Doc 9303 Part 11, Appendix D (BAC).
